osure rule:** only files present under `./osng/` participate. Discover them via `graph.*` links. Sibling branches that were not snapshotted are simply absent — do not invent or fetch them from elsewhere.\n\n## Strategy (how to traverse via graph.*)\nstrategy_id: outline_then_fill\nUse Standard / Root / Mid / Leaf roles from the subgraph. Do not invent claims absent from OSN text you opened.\n- **Pass 1 (outline, ancestor-first):** walk Root then `graph.child_osn_ids` pre-order; write OUTLINE.md / FILE_PLAN.md only (titles + owning OSN ids) — no full body yet.\n- **Pass 2 (fill, descendant-first):** walk children before parents within each chapter/module; fill artifact bodies from leaf `output_spec` text.\n- **Pass 3 (reconcile):** re-open Root (+ Standard if in scope); fix global consistency against success evidences.\n- At each node: open the YAML under `./osng/`, read the header if needed, then extract `seed`, `output_spec`, `thematic_lenses`, `success_evidences`, and `graph` as needed for the artifact.\n- Resolve `id` / `file_name` to a snapshotted `*.osn.yaml` under `./osng/` (directory layout mirrors Lexiom_1_3; `graph.*` remains authoritative).\n- Do not paste or assume OSN bodies from memory; pull requirements from the files you open.\n\n## Artifact contract\n- Primary deliverable: document.md (coherent entry document).\n- Optional multi-file pack under sections/ only if Root output_spec or the outline demands it.\n- **Outcome cleanliness (required):** document.md and sections/** must be free of OSNG/OSN traces — no OSN ids, *.osn.yaml paths, schema field names (output_spec, seed, graph.*, success_evidences, …), build/process meta, or “compiled from OSN…” language. Write finished domain prose only.\n- Provenance (which OSN informed which section) belongs ONLY in BUILD_REPORT.md; OUTLINE.md may keep owning OSN ids as Lexiom scaffold — never copy those into the reader-facing body.\n- Before finish: scan the outcome body and remove any residual OSNG/OSN traces (plugin failure if any remain).\n- Pass 1: write OUTLINE.md (TOC + owning OSN ids as scaffold only); no full body copy.\n- Pass 2: fill document.md (and optional sections/) in reader-facing voice — no OSNG traces.\n- Pass 3: reconcile Root/Standard tone and success evidences; run cleanliness scan on the outcome body.\n- Always write BUILD_REPORT.md listing included OSN ids you actually used, strategy, primary files, gaps, and which OSN supplied each major decision.\n\n## Non-goals\n- Not a coding agent; do not emit application source trees.\n- Do not invent unsupported claims.\n- Do not modify files under ./osng/ (snapshot is read-only).\n- Do not treat this prompt as a restatement of OSN schema — use OSN headers.\n- Do not publish OSNG/OSN process, ids, or schema vocabulary inside document.md / sections/.\n\n## Conflict precedence (when Concordance is unavailable)\n- Standard ancestor invariants\n- Compilation root outcome contract\n- Mid-level structural OSNs (chapters/parts)\n- Leaf OSNs (detailed messaging / clauses)\n- Record unresolved conflicts in BUILD_REPORT.md rather than inventing a silent merge.\n\n## Extraction protocol\n1. Read compilation-root header + `./OSNG_Basics_README.md`.\n2. Traverse via graph.* among files under `./osng/`, using strategy_id walk rules above.\n3. For each visited OSN, extract only what the artifact needs (prefer `output_spec`; use `seed` for intent). Do not collect evidence files here.\n4. Produce the artifact at the project root.\n5. Write BUILD_REPORT.md with provenance (OSN id → contribution).\n\n## Agent execution\n- Inspect source files through the CA workspace tools; do not assume contents from filenames.\n- Write primary artifacts through the CA workspace tools and finish only after verification.\n- Evidence generation remains a separate Step 5 pass described by `EVIDENCE_AGENT_PROMPT.md`.\n"
